Subject: [PATCH] Resolve remaining duplicate/colliding class names outside
 intelligence/

The consolidation report only ever scanned inside intelligence/, so it
missed four collisions elsewhere in the codebase:

- ConversationArtifact (conversations/parser.py vs conversations/importer.py):
  different shapes (source_path/title/content_length vs messages/keywords).
  Unrelated concepts sharing a name -> renamed the importer.py one to
  ParsedConversation.

- Artifact (models.py vs registry/artifact_registry.py): models.py's version
  isn't used anywhere outside its own test; registry's version is the one
  actually used in production (repository/mapper.py). Renamed the unused
  one to ArtifactRecord.

- ArchiveArtifact (reconstruction/archive_engine.py vs archive/connector.py):
  same concept (a file found while scanning a directory), same core fields,
  only a third bonus field differed (size vs name). True duplicate -> merged
  into a new archive/models.py as the single source of truth; both callers
  now import from there.

- ImportedArtifact (importer/models.py vs archive/importer.py): similar
  field names but incompatible artifact_type vocabularies (format labels
  vs content categories) and separate id schemes. Unrelated concepts
  sharing a name -> renamed the archive/importer.py one to
  ArchiveImportRecord; left importer/models.py's version (used by the
  production ingestion pipeline) untouched.

245 tests passing before and after.
